Raisse the Thaumaturge <raisse@valdyas.org> writes:

> No; the ring of slow digestion prevents all normal hunger, but *not*
> extra hunger from rings, *including itself*. Wearing two rings of slow
> digestion doesn't make you less normal-hungry, but it does make you
> twice as extra-hungry.

The ring-hunger doesn't happen at the same time for both rings.
Instead, you first get hit by the ring on your right hand and then a
couple of turns later by the ring on the left hand. This is based on
the global time counter. (Or at least this is what I've been led to
believe, I haven't read the sources myself). If you remember to always
remove the ring that is going to fire next and put it back just after
the hunger check is done, then you don't get hungry at all.

However, this way you will be spending about 20% of your playing time
swapping rings...

